<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10422"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:topsailgrl@yahoo.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Topsailgrl<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Topsailgrl<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 04, 2005 - 4:26 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I hope you are right Johno and have a feeling that you are. I dont know alot about the Lutheran Church.  <BR> <BR>I didnt mean to strike  up a religous debate but If it can be done without people going nuts I guess it&#39;s ok. Seems like there are two things that can get people really fired up and hatefull and thats religion and abortion. Two very volitile subjects.  <BR> <BR>Bmodule-no, we dont have to answer the door! One thing I have never been able to understand about the Jehovah&#39;s......If they honestly believe that only 144,000 are going to heaven, then why are they still recruiting??? I would be like this...I got my ticket, you worry about yours! The tickets are bound to be sold out by now!  <BR> <BR>I agree Lostdog-and Oaklahoma Mike-He is just manipulating the good Rev and the church! <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10422-->
<!--Post: 10452--><!--Time: 1109963232-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10452"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 04, 2005 - 11:07 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->B - No we don&#39;t! I think the First Amendment has something to do with it!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10452-->
<!--Post: 10495--><!--Time: 1109973391-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10495"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 04, 2005 - 1:56 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I wonder how much redemption the good Rev would feel if it was his baby daughter bound, gagged, hung up, and gutted from a rafter ? How willing would he be to redeem the soul of a souless killer if the victim was his own family ?  <BR> <BR>It is always easiest to redeem those who have not truly touched you.  .  .  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10495-->
<!--Post: 10500--><!--Time: 1109974567-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10500"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lostdog<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lostdog<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 04, 2005 - 2:16 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Funny, no one profiled BTK as a door to door proselytizer. <BR> <BR>Talk about a Watchtower to watch from without being watched. <BR> <BR>Hmmm… “a well dressed man” … a bag or briefcase… <BR> <BR>Apologies to any J.W.s out there. You guys take enough flack as it is… plus the whole doorknocking, pioneering thing probably doesn’t play too well in the Wichita metro area these days. <BR> <BR>Sorry. <BR> <BR>One question… where do you go to the bathroom? <BR> <BR>_ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _  _ <BR> <BR>Reverend Mike, are you out there? <BR> <BR>Within days it will become clear that you were a piece of meat stitched into the leatherface you came to know and admire as President Dennis. <BR> <BR>Running a good church has immeasurable rewards. It is also a hard headache of inconsolable widows, baby funerals, shotgun weddings and money troubles. It can be hellabad lonely too. <BR> <BR>Here was a guy who made things easier. You could depend on him. He was punctual and quick to pull out his checkbook.  He was a problem solver. I’ll bet he treated you like a man – not a man of God. You could be yourself around him. He grasped your right hand firmly with both of his and looked you deep in the eye…He was staunch, upright, impeccable, devout. <BR> <BR>Masterful. <BR> <BR>“When in the House of the Lord, I am a Saint.  <BR>In uniform, I am a martinet. <BR>At the head of my table, I am a leader.  <BR>When I prowl, when I write, when I fantasize, <BR>when I pounce, when I hit,  when I collect, <BR> I am Bind, Torture, Kill.” <BR> <BR>…A one man show, a costume tragedy with you in the chorus, Mike. <BR> <BR>You are the living victim of evil incarnate. You are the spiritual leader of a character actor. Those were the roles he assigned to you. <BR> <BR>The Dennis you loved was a hollow audio-animatronic, hardwired by the devil himself. <BR>The phantom who betrayed all of God’s creation is in a freefall powered by the unforgiving gravity of evil. <BR> <BR>That’s the best explanation I can offer to you. <BR>President Dennis can’t explain. Would you listen if he tried to? <BR> <BR>Christ has the answer… and you know Him. He will withhold it. <BR>He’ll guide you and monitor your growth.  <BR>He’ll watch from the wings as you privately question your faith. <BR>He’ll understand your struggle with forgiveness. <BR>The parent still looks to their middle aged child for signs of improvement. <BR> <BR>His instructions are simple, it’s the practice that’s complex. <BR> <BR>As for the phantom, there is no soul to save. <BR>Jesus may plan to shovel up President Dennis’ splattered remains and mold a new heart in his perfect hands… but the fall is far from over.  <BR> <BR>He fooled you. He cannot fool The Christ. <BR> <BR> <BR>I will pray for you Mike – for the Dietz family and your flock – just as I’ve prayed for his victims, living and dead, known and unknown. <BR> <BR>Peace. <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR>  <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10500-->
<!--Post: 10523--><!--Time: 1109981911-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10523"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lctrip<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lctrip<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 04, 2005 - 4:18 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->LDog, while I &#40;respectfully&#41; disagreed with your thoughts regarding Rader&#39;s backyard I think this latest post on this thread is outstanding and on the mark.  Wish I had your talent for expressing my thoughts.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
